Z||000000||KRMFiero||08-14-2001||09:24 PM||||Okay I got my engine mounts from Joe today, I installed them, I went to install Trans mounts and they are off about 1" to the front and about 1" to the right side, I fooled with it, I got the front Trans mount in, the rear one i cant, seems to be lined up but bracket needs to be about 1" to the right for me to be able to put the bolts on. Also the engine/Trans doenst seem to be exactly straigt, it seems to be about a 1/2" difference from both sides (messured to center of front cradle mounts) the side where the trans connects to engine is what is 1/2" closer to front.<P>I e-mailed Joe he told me i do not have to slot anything with the Mounts I have, but i think i have to; what do I do? <P>I have:<BR>Late 1989 Caddy Seville Trans/Engine<BR>1987 Buick Overdrive Trans mounts/brackets<BR>Joe's mounts with the Energy suspention mount attached<BR>And when i get it done i have 1989 Ponitac 6000 OD LD axles to install<P>Any ideas? Rockcrawl you say i have to slot them, Joe says no... Im thinking i have to slot them though HELP ME PLEASE AHH.<P>Kyle||||reg||1
Z||000001||rockcrawl||08-15-2001||07:09 AM||||I think the holes for the rear trans mount need to be moved or slotted to the right about 1.25'. Maybe Joe thinks you're using a three speed? I've never used his mounts. If you want the trans (and engine) to sit straight, you'll need to move the rear holes.<P>I think my blue V8 is running well enough to take to the Dutch Classic this weekend...WooHoo!! ||||reg||1
